 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOpenID Connect grant dispatchers assign wrong handlers\n\n#### Description\n\nThe OpenID Connect grant dispatchers are incorrectly assigning handlers due to swapped parameter assignments in their constructors. This causes OAuth2 requests to be handled by OpenID Connect handlers and vice versa.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.openid.connect.core.grant_types.dispatchers import AuthorizationCodeGrantDispatcher\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.grant_types import AuthorizationCodeGrant as OAuth2AuthorizationCodeGrant\nfrom oauthlib.openid.connect.core.grant_types import AuthorizationCodeGrant\n\n# Create dispatcher with OAuth2 as default and OpenID as oidc handler\noauth2_grant = OAuth2AuthorizationCodeGrant()\noidc_grant = AuthorizationCodeGrant()\ndispatcher = AuthorizationCodeGrantDispatcher(default_grant=oauth2_grant, oidc_grant=oidc_grant)\n\n# Create a regular OAuth2 request (no openid scope)\nclass MockRequest:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.scopes = ['read', 'write']\n\nrequest = MockRequest()\nhandler = dispatcher._handler_for_request(request)\n\n# This should return the OAuth2 handler but returns the OpenID handler instead\nprint(f\"Expected: {OAuth2AuthorizationCodeGrant}\")\nprint(f\"Got: {type(handler)}\")\n```\n\nThe issue affects all three dispatcher classes:\n- `AuthorizationCodeGrantDispatcher`\n- `ImplicitTokenGrantDispatcher` \n- `AuthorizationTokenGrantDispatcher`\n\nRegular OAuth2 requests are being routed to OpenID Connect handlers when they should use the default OAuth2 handlers, and OpenID Connect requests may not be handled properly.\n</issue>\n",
